    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Draw a number line marked with the whole numbers from 0 to 3, and indicate on it where the markers for $\\frac{2}{3}$, $\\frac{1}{6}$, $\\frac{8}{9}$, $2\\frac{5}{6}$, $1\\frac{1}{9}$ and $\\frac{11}{6}$ are located.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "From left to right: $\\frac{1}{6},\\ \\frac{2}{3},\\ \\frac{8}{9},\\ 1\\frac{1}{9},\\ \\frac{11}{6},\\ 2\\frac{5}{6}$.",
      "worked": "Divide each unit interval into 18 equal subintervals so that sixths, thirds and ninths can all be marked exactly.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{6}&=\\frac{3}{18}\\\\\\frac{2}{3}&=\\frac{12}{18}\\\\\\frac{8}{9}&=\\frac{16}{18}\\\\1\\frac{1}{9}&=1\\frac{2}{18}\\\\\\frac{11}{6}&=1\\frac{5}{6}=1\\frac{15}{18}\\\\2\\frac{5}{6}&=2\\frac{15}{18}\\end{align*}$$\n\nMark each number at its corresponding subdivision, as shown.",
